;; The module _remote_debugging (queue 296, 293's DECISION 1 (a); CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_remote_debugging_module.c
;; and Python/remote_debug.h): its names, so that asyncio.tools imports (python -m asyncio's REPL, test_repl's asyncio
;; rows, test_asyncio.test_tools' pure functions) and test_external_inspection runs. The five structseq types (TaskInfo,
;; FrameInfo, CoroInfo, ThreadInfo, AwaitedInfo) as CPython's; PROCESS_VM_READV_SUPPORTED 0 (pyi reads no process's
;; memory). RemoteUnwinder(pid, *, all_threads=False, only_active_thread=False, debug=False) checks its arguments as
;; RemoteUnwinder.__init__ does, then fails as CPython's Linux search fails on a process that holds no PyRuntime
;; section (search_linux_map_for_section): /proc/PID/maps unreadable is the OSError of its errno with the
;; "Cannot open process memory map file" OSError raised from it; then RuntimeError "Failed to find the PyRuntime section
;; in process PID on Linux platform" (its context the OSError, if any), and with debug=True "Failed to get Python runtime
;; address" raised from it. Left out: reading a process's frames (another pyi's are Go's, not CPython's PyRuntime; a
;; CPython's would need its debug offsets read through /proc/PID/mem): get_stack_trace, get_all_awaited_by and
;; get_async_stack_trace exist but no unwinder reaches them initialized (an instance made by __new__ alone raises).

